  "question": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int_{\\pi / 4}^{\\pi / 3} \\frac{\\sin x}{x} d x$. Then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\leq 1 \\leq 1$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$4 \\leq 1 \\leq 2 \\sqrt{30}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\leq 1 \\leq \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$1 \\leq 1 \\leq \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{2}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\n$$\r\nI=\\int_{\\pi / 4}^{\\pi / 3} \\frac{\\sin x}{x} d x\r\n$$\r\nsince, $\\frac{\\sin x}{x}$ is a decreasing function.\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{c}\r\n\\frac{\\pi}{12} \\times \\frac{\\sin \\pi / 3}{\\pi / 3} \\leq 1 \\leq \\frac{\\pi}{12} \\times \\frac{\\sin \\pi / 4}{\\pi / 4} \\\\\r\n\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\leq I \\leq \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$"
  }
}